### Food Delivery API endpoint tests
### Run the services first. Direct service URLs use launchSettings ports.
### Seeded login password for all seeded accounts: Admin@123
### After each login, copy response.data.accessToken into the matching token variable.

@auth = http://localhost:55427
@users = http://localhost:5213
@delivery = http://localhost:5248
@gateway = http://localhost:8080

@adminUserId = 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555
@customerUserId = aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa
@merchantUserId = bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb
@shipperUserId = 99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999

@merchantId = cccccccc-cccc-cccc-cccc-cccccccccccc
@customerAddressId = dddddddd-dddd-dddd-dddd-dddddddddddd
@merchantAddressId = ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff
@shipperId = 56565656-5656-5656-5656-565656565656
@assignmentId = 64444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444
@orderId = 62222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

@adminToken = paste-admin-access-token-here
@customerToken = paste-customer-access-token-here
@merchantToken = paste-merchant-access-token-here
@shipperToken = paste-shipper-access-token-here

### ---------------- AuthenticationService ----------------

### Login admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@fooddelivery.local",
  "password": "Admin@123",
  "deviceName": "manual-http"
}

### Login customer
# @name loginCustomer
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@fooddelivery.local",
  "password": "Admin@123",
  "deviceName": "manual-http"
}

### Login merchant
# @name loginMerchant
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "merchant@fooddelivery.local",
  "password": "Admin@123",
  "deviceName": "manual-http"
}

### Login shipper
# @name loginShipper
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "shipper@fooddelivery.local",
  "password": "Admin@123",
  "deviceName": "manual-http"
}

### Register a new customer
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.customer+{{$timestamp}}@fooddelivery.local",
  "password": "Admin@123",
  "fullName": "Manual Test Customer"
}

### Verify OTP - replace email and otp with values from DB/email/RabbitMQ consumer log
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.customer@example.local",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### Resend OTP
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/resend-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.customer@example.local"
}

### Refresh token - paste response.data.refreshToken from login
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "paste-refresh-token-here",
  "deviceName": "manual-http"
}

### Logout - paste a valid refresh token
POST {{auth}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "paste-refresh-token-here",
  "deviceName": "manual-http"
}

### ---------------- UserService: users and files ----------------

### Admin: get all users
GET {{users}}/api/users?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Customer: get own profile
GET {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Customer: update own profile
PUT {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Seeded Customer Updated",
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatars/customer-updated.png"
}

### Customer: get own addresses
GET {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}/addresses?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Customer: get one own address
GET {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}/addresses/{{customerAddressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Customer: add address
POST {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressLine": "10 Test Street",
  "ward": "Ben Nghe",
  "district": "District 1",
  "city": "Ho Chi Minh City",
  "lat": 10.7769,
  "lng": 106.7009,
  "label": "Manual Test",
  "recipientName": "Seeded Customer",
  "phone": "0900000099",
  "isDefault": false
}

### Customer: update address
PUT {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}/addresses/{{customerAddressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressLine": "1 Nguyen Hue Updated",
  "ward": "Ben Nghe",
  "district": "District 1",
  "city": "Ho Chi Minh City",
  "lat": 10.7769,
  "lng": 106.7009,
  "label": "Home",
  "recipientName": "Seeded Customer",
  "phone": "0900000001",
  "isDefault": true
}

### User file upload URL
GET {{users}}/api/files/get-upload-url?fileName=avatar.png&contentType=image/png
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Customer: delete own address - destructive; prefer using an address created by the add-address request
DELETE {{users}}/api/users/{{customerUserId}}/addresses/replace-created-address-id
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Admin/customer: delete user - destructive; do not run against seeded accounts unless you plan to reseed
DELETE {{users}}/api/users/replace-user-id
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------- UserService: merchant ----------------

### Customer: request merchant role
POST {{users}}/api/users/merchant-request
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storeName": "Manual Test Store",
  "storeDescription": "A test merchant request.",
  "businessLicense": "BL-MANUAL-001",
  "businessLicenseUrl": "https://example.com/licenses/manual.jpg",
  "taxId": "TAX-MANUAL-001"
}

### Admin: get merchant requests
GET {{users}}/api/users/merchant-request?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Admin: review merchant request - replace request id
PATCH {{users}}/api/users/merchant-request/replace-request-id/review
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "verificationStatus": 1,
  "rejectedReason": null
}

### Authenticated: get merchants
GET {{users}}/api/users/merchants?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Authenticated: get merchant by id
GET {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Authenticated: get merchant location
GET {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}/location?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Merchant owner: get merchant addresses
GET {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}/addresses?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Merchant owner: get merchant address by id
GET {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}/addresses/{{merchantAddressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Merchant owner: add merchant address
POST {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressLine": "20 Manual Store Street",
  "ward": "Ben Thanh",
  "district": "District 1",
  "city": "Ho Chi Minh City",
  "lat": 10.7722,
  "lng": 106.6983
}

### Merchant owner: update merchant address
PUT {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}/addresses/{{merchantAddressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressLine": "2 Le Loi Updated",
  "ward": "Ben Thanh",
  "district": "District 1",
  "city": "Ho Chi Minh City",
  "lat": 10.7722,
  "lng": 106.6983
}

### Merchant owner: update merchant
PUT {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storeName": "Seeded Merchant Store Updated",
  "storeDescription": "Updated from manual HTTP test.",
  "storeLogoUrl": "https://example.com/stores/logo-updated.png",
  "storeBannerUrl": "https://example.com/stores/banner-updated.png",
  "businessLicense": "BL-SEED-0001",
  "taxId": "TAX-SEED-0001",
  "isOpen": true,
  "openingTime": "08:00:00",
  "closingTime": "22:00:00",
  "minOrderAmount": 30000,
  "avgPrepTime": 20,
  "status": 1
}

### Merchant owner: delete merchant address - destructive; prefer using an address created by add-merchant-address
DELETE {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}/addresses/replace-created-merchant-address-id
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Merchant owner/admin: delete merchant - destructive; do not run against seeded merchant unless you plan to reseed
DELETE {{users}}/api/users/merchants/{{merchantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{merchantToken}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------- UserService: shipper ----------------

### Customer: request shipper role
POST {{users}}/api/users/shipper-request
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "licenseNumber": "DL-MANUAL-001",
  "licenseFrontUrl": "https://example.com/shipper/license-front.jpg",
  "licenseBackUrl": "https://example.com/shipper/license-back.jpg",
  "idCardFrontUrl": "https://example.com/shipper/id-front.jpg",
  "idCardBackUrl": "https://example.com/shipper/id-back.jpg",
  "selfieUrl": "https://example.com/shipper/selfie.jpg",
  "idNumber": "079202600099",
  "fullName": "Manual Test Shipper",
  "dateOfBirth": "1998-04-12T00:00:00Z"
}

### Admin: get shipper requests
GET {{users}}/api/users/shipper-request?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Admin: review shipper request - replace request id
PATCH {{users}}/api/users/shipper-request/replace-request-id/review
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "verificationStatus": 1,
  "rejectedReason": null
}

### Public: get shippers
GET {{users}}/api/users/shippers?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### Public: get shipper by id
GET {{users}}/api/users/shippers/{{shipperId}}
Accept: application/json

### Shipper owner: update shipper
PUT {{users}}/api/users/shippers/{{shipperId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehiclePlate": "59A-123.45",
  "status": 1
}

### Shipper owner/admin: delete shipper - destructive; do not run against seeded shipper unless you plan to reseed
DELETE {{users}}/api/users/shippers/{{shipperId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------- DeliveryService ----------------

### Admin: get all availabilities
GET {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/availabilities?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Shipper: get own availability
GET {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/shippers/{{shipperId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Shipper: toggle availability
POST {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/availability/toggle?shipperId={{shipperId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isGoOnline": true,
  "lat": 10.7735,
  "lng": 106.6975
}

### Shipper: update location
POST {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "shipperId": "{{shipperId}}",
  "latitude": 10.7735,
  "longitude": 106.6975
}

### Admin: get all assignments
GET {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/assignments?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Customer or shipper: get assignment by id
GET {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/assignments/{{assignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Shipper: get own assignments
GET {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/shippers/{{shipperId}}/assignments?pageIndex=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Shipper: accept/reject assignment
POST {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/assignments/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assignmentId": "{{assignmentId}}",
  "isAccepted": true,
  "rejectReason": null
}

### Shipper: update assignment status
POST {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/assignments/{{assignmentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PickedUp",
  "note": "Picked up from merchant.",
  "proofFileKey": "deliveries/{{orderId}}/{{shipperId}}/pickup/manual-proof.jpg"
}

### Shipper: delivery upload URL
GET {{delivery}}/api/deliveries/files/upload-url?orderId={{orderId}}&shipperId={{shipperId}}&stage=pickup&fileName=proof.jpg&contentType=image/jpeg
Authorization: Bearer {{shipperToken}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------- NotificationService ----------------
### NotificationService has no HTTP controllers currently.
### Test it by publishing RabbitMQ events that it consumes:
### - otp.send-requested
### - lockedout
### - order.completed
### - shipper.found
### - delivery.milestone
### Then verify NotificationService logs, emails, and notification database rows.
